  "id": "self-activity",
  "term": "self-activity",
  "definition": "Self-activity, also called immanent activity, is a course of change that appears to arise within the thing itself rather than being mainly produced by outside influences. In psychology and biology, it refers to changes in the organism or mind that seem internally determined or self-directing.",
